{%- comment -%}
  sp-nutrition-facts-pouch.liquid — FDA-format Nutrition Facts for The Pouch (1 pouch = 100 g).
  Values: Eurofins AR-25-R2-020720-01 (batch 2025-08-01, Brix 12) + SGS CDF25-0005113-02A2 (same batch: calcium, iron).
  Rounding per 21 CFR 101.9(c). All values scaled to finished Brix 11 (measured at Brix 12 x 11/12), Kev 2026-09-20. Calories = 4-4-9 with insoluble fiber excluded and soluble fiber at 2 kcal/g,
  assuming a 50/50 split until the AOAC 991.43 split is measured (same method as the Shot panel).
  Single source: Pouch-100g-US-Nutrition-Facts-v1-2026-09-17.md (repo root).
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="sp-nf" aria-label="Nutrition Facts">
  <div class="t">Nutrition Facts</div>
  <div class="sm">1 serving per container</div>
  <div class="r med"><b>Serving size</b><b>1 pouch (100 g)</b></div>
  <div class="sm" style="padding-top:4px"><b>Amount per serving</b></div>
  <div class="cal"><span class="l">Calories</span><span class="n">25</span></div>
  <div class="dv">% Daily Value*</div>
  <div class="r"><span><b>Total Fat</b> 0g</span><b>0%</b></div>
  <div class="r in"><span>Saturated Fat 0g</span><b>0%</b></div>
  <div class="r in"><span>Trans Fat 0g</span><span></span></div>
  <div class="r"><span><b>Cholesterol</b> 0mg</span><b>0%</b></div>
  <div class="r"><span><b>Sodium</b> 0mg</span><b>0%</b></div>
  <div class="r"><span><b>Total Carbohydrate</b> 12g</span><b>4%</b></div>
  <div class="r in"><span>Dietary Fiber 10g</span><b>36%</b></div>
  <div class="r in"><span>Total Sugars 2g</span><span></span></div>
  <div class="r in2"><span>Includes 0g Added Sugars</span><b>0%</b></div>
  <div class="r thick"><span><b>Protein</b> 1g</span><span></span></div>
  <div class="r"><span>Vitamin D 0mcg</span><span>0%</span></div>
  <div class="r"><span>Calcium 40mg</span><span>4%</span></div>
  <div class="r"><span>Iron 0mg</span><span>0%</span></div>
  <div class="r med"><span>Potassium 380mg</span><span>8%</span></div>
  <div class="foot">* The % Daily Value (DV) tells you how much a nutrient in a serving of food contributes to a daily diet. 2,000 calories a day is used for general nutrition advice.</div>
</div>
